Site Note: Station Odufor, Etche LGA.

The interpreted geophysical model for Station Odufor consists of four layers. The resistivity starts low at 20.32 $\Omega$m, increases through the second layer (851.16 $\Omega$m) to a maximum in the third layer (2511.9 $\Omega$m), and subsequently drops to 1345 $\Omega$m in the fourth layer. Applying the curve-type notation rules, the first three layers form an 'A' pattern ($r_1 < r_2 < r_3$), and the sequence of the second, third, and fourth layers forms a 'K' pattern ($r_2 < r_3 > r_4$). This results in an AK-type curve, which is consistent with the label provided in the published survey.

